Today, I continued developing my AI-powered vision assistant by integrating Ray-Ban Meta smart glasses with YOLO11 object detection, OpenAI Vision LLM, and voice interaction using Python.

I successfully implemented real-time object detection through the glasses' video feed and connected the system to an OpenAI vision model capable of interpreting captured images and answering natural-language questions.

During development, I resolved several technical issues involving ONNX model compatibility, Python dependencies, API authentication, and microphone integration using PyAudioWPatch.

I also implemented automatic scene narration and worked on improving text-to-speech playback so the AI can respond verbally to multiple questions. Repeated voice playback is still being tested.

The next goal is to enable hands-free voice interaction, improve object localization, and eventually integrate the vision system with the Epson VT6 robotic arm for assistive robotics applications.

Current status: Real-time YOLO detection and LLM image understanding are working. Voice interaction is implemented and undergoing further testing. Robot movement remains disabled.


